-- title:
--   Normalised connecting idele between two maximal orders
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and let $q'$ be a prime such that the quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ is definite and ramified exactly at $q'$, in the sense that $a<0$, $b<0$ and, for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, every nonzero element of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ is a unit precisely when $q'$ lies in $v$. Let $\Lambda_1,\Lambda_2$ be $\mathbb{Z}$-submodules of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ which are maximal orders, i.e. each contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, is finitely generated, spans $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, and is the only order containing it. Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number with $q'\nmid N$ such that the index of the additive group $\Lambda_1\cap\Lambda_2$ in $\Lambda_1$ equals $N$. Then there is a unit $m$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},\mathrm{fin}}$, where $\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},\mathrm{fin}}$ is the finite adele ring of $\mathbb{Q}$, such that: the submodule of elements of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ whose image in the adelic algebra lies in $m\,\widehat{\Lambda_1}\,m^{-1}$ is exactly $\Lambda_2$; $m$ lies in $\widehat{\Lambda_1}$, the additive subgroup generated by the elements $z\otimes\alpha$ with $z\in\Lambda_1$ and $\alpha$ an everywhere integral finite adele; and $N\cdot m^{-1}$ also lies in $\widehat{\Lambda_1}$.
--
--   This is the refinement, for a definite quaternion algebra over $\mathbb{Q}$ ramified at a single prime, of the fact that any two maximal orders are conjugate by a finite idele: the connecting idele can be normalised to be integral with respect to the first order and to have $N$ times its inverse integral as well, $N$ being the index of $\Lambda_1\cap\Lambda_2$ in $\Lambda_1$. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfel'd tower to exhibit intersections of two maximal orders as Eichler orders of level $N$ and to compare degeneracy and Hecke operators at that level.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_QuaternionAlgebra_exists_conjByFiniteIdele_eq_mem_finiteAdeleBox_smul_inv_mem_of_relIndex_eq.lean

